# leads: forming and trimming at the bench (decision C15). The DIP in
# the vise legs up; the rig bends the resistor's lead 1 and shears it,
# and the arm lays its end alongside pin 3's leg (a lap joint, decision
# C22); pincer P1 holds it there and the iron station solders it; pincer
# P2 bends the resistor's other lead down, round a mandrel 3 mm from its
# body, toward where its next part will be; the turntable presents that
# lead to the cutter station S4, which trims it to 8 mm -- the rest
# falls into the bin; P1 lets go and the resistor stays, soldered on.
reset circuit=lap
tool A tweezers
pick A U1 grasp=ends
place A U1 at=0,0,-24 rpy=180,0,90
vise close
release A U1
pick A R1 grasp=body
lift A mm=60
insert A on=R1.1 at=12
form angle=90
lift A mm=30
shear A on=R1.1 at=17.2
lift A mm=60
bring A R1.1 to=U1.3.tip along=-0.934,0.356,0 lap=3.2
pinch P1 on=R1.1 at=3
release A R1
lift A mm=60
present U1.3+R1.1 at=S1
scope aim=U1.3+R1.1 zoom=8
touch S1 at=U1.3+R1.1 dwell=2
feed S1 mm=2 rate=1
back S1
wait until=U1.3+R1.1 below=100
scope aim=R1.2 zoom=4
bend P2 on=R1.2 at=3 angle=90 toward=0,0,-1
present R1.2.8 at=S4
trim S4 on=R1.2 at=8
unpinch P1
